        <briefdescription>
<para>Variants of check performed on an authenticated pointer. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>In cases such as authenticating the LR value when performing a tail call or when re-signing a signed pointer with a different signing schema, a failed authentication may not generate an exception on its own and may create an authentication or signing oracle if not checked explicitly.</para>
<para>A number of check methods modify control flow in a similar way by rewriting the code</para>
<para><computeroutput> &lt;authenticate LR&gt; &lt;more instructions&gt; </computeroutput></para>
<para>as follows:</para>
<para>``` &lt;authenticate LR&gt; &lt;method-specific checker&gt; on_fail: brk <computeroutput> on_success: &lt;more instructions&gt;</computeroutput></para>
<para><computeroutput> ``` enum class AuthCheckMethod { Do not check the value at all </computeroutput></para>
        </detaileddescription>
